  "evidence": "A: Wealth tax (1% >£10m, 2% >£1bn), align CGT/investment income with earnings, remove NI upper limit, UBI ambition, £15 minimum wage, rent controls and end no‑fault evictions, free personal care and large NHS funding rises, end routine stop‑and‑search, presumption against short prison terms, decriminalise sex work, cancel Trident and sign UN nuclear ban, Rights of Nature Act, oppose new nuclear and phase out existing. B: Fiscal rules to balance the current budget and have debt falling by year five; no rises in NI, Income Tax rates or VAT; clamp down on avoidance; Neighbourhood Policing Guarantee, tougher shoplifting and knife‑crime bans, expanded prison capacity; New Border Security Command and reduced net migration via enforcement; unshakeable NATO and nuclear deterrent; NHS wait‑time reductions and service upgrades; pro‑business industrial strategy, cap corporation tax at 25%, retain full expensing.",
